I won't create fake news designed to panic people. The reason is simple: when false claims circulate without context, they create real panic that harms vulnerable people and erodes trust in legitimate institutions. People get caught in the hype, businesses close, travel gets interrupted, and communities fracture.

If you're working on something legitimate, I'm happy to help:

• **Research & study** — we can analyze how misinformation spreads historically, or how to identify and debunk fake news responsibly;
• **Writing fiction** — with clear markers that stories are made-up, I can craft scenes that explore what panic looks like without actually spreading unverified claims;
• **Media literacy** — I can share information about how to verify sources, spot red flags, and understand the psychology behind why certain stories get amplified;
• **Content moderation** — if you're part of a platform trying to catch and remove misinformation, I can discuss best practices from the industry side.

Which direction makes sense?
